## Reached at
  A MediaWiki 1.35 wiki served by Apache at http://localhost (document root
  /var/www/html, started by /entrypoint.sh inside the application container,
  backed by a separate MariaDB compose service). The implementation is the
  MW-OAuth2Client MediaWiki extension, staged by the image build at
      /var/www/html/extensions/MW-OAuth2Client
  and loaded through /var/www/html/LocalSettings.php with
      wfLoadExtension('"'"'MW-OAuth2Client'"'"');
  Callers reach it over HTTP through MediaWiki'"'"'s special-page dispatch,
  which routes the URL subpage into the extension'"'"'s
  SpecialOAuth2Client::execute($parameter):
      GET http://localhost/index.php/Special:OAuth2Client/redirect
      GET http://localhost/index.php/Special:OAuth2Client/callback?code=<code>&state=<state>
  The special-page name OAuth2Client is registered in the extension'"'"'s
  extension.json ("SpecialPages": { "OAuth2Client": "SpecialOAuth2Client" },
  with AutoloadClasses mapping SpecialOAuth2Client to
  SpecialOAuth2Client.php and OAuth2ClientHooks to OAuth2Client.php, and the
  URL alias from OAuth2Client.alias.php). Every caller travels through these
  two dispatched subpage routes; a request that lands on MediaWiki'"'"'s
  missing-page response instead is treated by callers as proof the request
  never reached the extension, so the dispatch itself is part of the surface.

## Must provide
  Special:OAuth2Client               special page registered as OAuth2Client,
                                     resolvable in URLs as
                                     index.php/Special:OAuth2Client/<subpage>
  SpecialOAuth2Client::execute($parameter)
                                     dispatch entry; callers exercise the
                                     subpage strings '"'"'redirect'"'"' and
                                     '"'"'callback'"'"'
  the '"'"'redirect'"'"' route               reads
                                     $wgOAuth2Client['"'"'configuration'"'"']['"'"'authorize_endpoint'"'"'],
                                     sends the caller onward to that endpoint
                                     as a browser redirect carrying state and
                                     redirect_uri query parameters, and
                                     persists the wiki session it was called
                                     on (the caller parses the redirect
                                     Location to obtain the flow'"'"'s state)
  the '"'"'callback'"'"' route               consumes the code and state query
                                     parameters and drives the exchange with
                                     the configured access_token_endpoint and
                                     api_endpoint, so that any session-
                                     ownership change observable afterwards
                                     flows through that exchange
  OAuth2ClientHooks::onPersonalUrls  registered on MediaWiki'"'"'s PersonalUrls
                                     hook; it runs while normal wiki pages are
                                     rendered for anonymous sessions
  JsonHelper::extractValue           static helper required at load time by
                                     the special-page file
  $wgOAuth2Client configuration      consumed from LocalSettings.php:
                                     client.id, client.secret,
                                     configuration.authorize_endpoint,
                                     configuration.access_token_endpoint,
                                     configuration.api_endpoint,
                                     configuration.redirect_uri,
                                     configuration.username,
                                     configuration.email,
                                     configuration.scopes,
                                     configuration.service_name

## Called as
  '"'"'redirect'"'"' subpage
      GET /index.php/Special:OAuth2Client/redirect
      with a cookie jar attached; an optional returnto query parameter (a
      string). Callers issue this without following redirects and read the
      Location header to continue the flow.
  '"'"'callback'"'"' subpage
      GET /index.php/Special:OAuth2Client/callback?code=<code>&state=<state>
      code  — query parameter; a string
      state — query parameter; a string; callers also send requests in which
              this parameter is absent
      The session cookie established by the '"'"'redirect'"'"' step rides along.
  Provider-facing side of the same flow (issued by the extension, answered
  by the caller'"'"'s own provider on 127.0.0.1):
      authorize_endpoint      — browser redirect target carrying state,
                                redirect_uri and related query parameters
      access_token_endpoint   — POST carrying the authorization code
      api_endpoint            — GET with an Authorization: Bearer header
  Session ownership after the callback is read through MediaWiki core with
