      GET /api.php?action=query&meta=userinfo&format=json

## Setup required
  - MediaWiki is installed at /var/www/html with LocalSettings.php generated
    by the container entrypoint on first start; the entrypoint also appends
    wfLoadExtension('"'"'MW-OAuth2Client'"'"') and an initial $wgOAuth2Client block.
  - Before exercising the flow, callers rewrite that $wgOAuth2Client block in
    /var/www/html/LocalSettings.php (inside a marked block they strip first
    and restore afterwards) so that authorize_endpoint, access_token_endpoint
    and api_endpoint point at their own provider on 127.0.0.1 and
    redirect_uri is
    http://localhost/index.php/Special:OAuth2Client/callback. The extension
    consumes these globals per request; PHP opcache revalidation can delay
    visibility of the rewritten file by up to about a minute.
  - Cookie-backed MediaWiki sessions must be live: the '"'"'redirect'"'"' route
    persists the session, and the '"'"'callback'"'"' route must land on the same
    session cookie.
  - The vendored OAuth2 client library must be present:
    extensions/MW-OAuth2Client/vendors/oauth2-client/vendor/autoload.php,
    installed by composer during the image build; the special page requires
    it at runtime and constructs a
    \League\OAuth2\Client\Provider\GenericProvider from the $wgOAuth2Client
    values.

