  elements name methods on the instantiated block. Each child element of an
  <action> supplies one argument to that call, passed as its text content; a
  block may carry several <action> elements. The method attribute and every
  argument value are strings.

## Setup required
  - The app must be installed and serving: /var/www/html/app/etc/local.xml
    exists (the container entrypoint runs the project'"'"'s install script against
    the MySQL instance before starting Apache).
  - Callers resolve the app and database from the environment: APP_URL,
    DB_HOST, DB_USER, DB_PASS, DB_NAME.
  - Callers delete the contents of /var/www/html/var/cache and
    /var/www/html/var/full_page_cache before every fetch, so rendering must
    follow the rows just written rather than any cached layout output. Both
    directories must exist and be writable (the image sets them 777).
  - /var/www/html/app/design/frontend/base/default/template exists in the app
    tree; callers place and remove short-lived files there during a run, so the
    tree stays writable by them.

## Test harness boundary
  A pytest runner (installed on the fly with uv) drives everything from inside
  the same container as the app: it opens its own MySQL connections to insert,
  read back, and delete cms_page rows; it wipes the cache directories by
  shelling out to rm -rf; it issues the HTTP GETs; and it inspects response
  bodies, database state, and files on disk around each fetch. It also creates
  and removes ephemeral files inside the app'"'"'s design tree. All of this is the
  calling side — none of it is part of the implementation, and none of it
  should be rebuilt.
