## 5. Required Interface Reachability Contract

This block states the required interface identity, resolution, invocation, input shape, and setup that the implementation must realize. It does not state expected outcomes, prescribe private implementation structure, or expand edit scope.

```text
test_interface = compiled/library (signals: ['"'"'absolute-path-static-archive'"'"', '"'"'compiled-c-harness'"'"', '"'"'ld-library-path'"'"', '"'"'subprocess-harness'"'"'])

This block states only where and how existing callers reach the implementation.
It does not state expected outcomes or prescribe implementation structure.

## Reached at
  The target lives in the PJSIP source tree staged by the image build at
  `/app` (working directory `/app`). The RTCP feedback parse/build entry
  points are defined in `/app/pjmedia/src/pjmedia/rtcp_fb.c` and compiled
  into the application'"'"'s own static archive:

      /app/pjmedia/lib/libpjmedia-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.a

  Callers never link a system copy. A C harness is compiled fresh on every
  run by `/usr/bin/gcc` with these include directories:

      -I/app/pjlib/include
      -I/app/pjlib-util/include
      -I/app/pjmedia/include
      -I/app/pjnath/include

  and linked against the application archives named by absolute path:

      /app/pjmedia/lib/libpjmedia-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.a
      /app/pjlib-util/lib/libpjlib-util-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.a
      /app/pjlib/lib/libpj-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.a
      /app/third_party/lib/libsrtp-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.a
      /app/third_party/lib/libresample-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.a

  followed by the system libraries `-lm -lpthread -lasound -luuid -lssl -lcrypto`.
  The header `/app/pjmedia/include/pjmedia/rtcp_fb.h` (which includes
  `pjmedia/rtcp.h`) declares the public surface; the harness sources it via
  `#include <pjmedia/rtcp_fb.h>` (and `#include <pjmedia/rtcp.h>` for the
  session type).

## Must provide
  All symbols below must resolve out of the linked archives (primarily
  `libpjmedia-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.a`); a missing symbol is a hard
  link failure the caller never skips.

  Parse functions (declared `PJ_DECL(pj_status_t)`, exported from the archive):
      pjmedia_rtcp_fb_parse_pli      function
      pjmedia_rtcp_fb_parse_nack     function
      pjmedia_rtcp_fb_parse_sli      function
      pjmedia_rtcp_fb_parse_rpsi     function

  Build functions (declared `PJ_DECL(pj_status_t)`, exported from the archive):
      pjmedia_rtcp_fb_build_pli      function
      pjmedia_rtcp_fb_build_nack      function
      pjmedia_rtcp_fb_build_sli      function
      pjmedia_rtcp_fb_build_rpsi     function

  Session lifecycle (declared in `pjmedia/rtcp.h`, exported from the same
  archive; the build harnesses call these to stand up a session first):
      pjmedia_rtcp_init              function, returns void
      pjmedia_rtcp_fini              function, returns void

  PJLIB lifecycle (exported from `libpj-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.a`; every
  harness calls `pj_init` before any RTCP call and `pj_shutdown` after):
      pj_init                        function
      pj_shutdown                    function

  Types the harness instantiates and reads fields from (declared in
  `pjmedia/rtcp_fb.h` / `pjmedia/rtcp.h`):
      pjmedia_rtcp_common            struct (fields pt, count, length, ssrc)
      pjmedia_rtcp_session           struct (passed by address to build_*)
