## 5. Required Interface Reachability Contract

This block states the required interface identity, resolution, invocation, input shape, and setup that the implementation must realize. It does not state expected outcomes, prescribe private implementation structure, or expand edit scope.

```text
test_interface = compiled/library (signals: ['"'"'compile-time-interface-assertion'"'"', '"'"'compiled-into-app-module'"'"', '"'"'go-test-runner'"'"', '"'"'reflective-method-call'"'"'])

This block states only where and how existing callers reach the implementation.
It does not state expected outcomes or prescribe implementation structure.

## Reached at
  The target is a Go application tree staged by the image build at /app. Its
  /app/go.mod declares the main module:
      module code.vegaprotocol.io/vega
  The callers compile a Go test package of their own into that module and link
  it against the module'"'"'s packages; every call below resolves through the
  module path with the working directory /app, run as:
      go test ./vsbharness/ -run '"'"'^<TestName>$'"'"' -v -count=1
  once per named Go test in the calling-side package, and
      go vet ./vsbharness/
  as a compile/link-consistency check on the same package. The directory
  /app/vsbharness holding that package is staged and wiped by the callers
  themselves; it is not part of the implementation.
  Module resolution must go through /app/go.mod alone: no Go workspace may be
  active (`go env GOWORK` reads empty), and each package imported by the
  calling-side package must resolve to a directory under /app/ — the callers
  check this with `go list -f '"'"'{{.Dir}}'"'"' <importpath>` run from /app. The Go
  toolchain is resolved by absolute path (/usr/local/go/bin/go, /usr/bin/go)
  with GOROOT=/usr/local/go, GOPATH=/go, GOMODCACHE=/go/pkg/mod.

